+def _empirical_cvar(losses, beta):
+    """
+    The conditional value at risk of an empirical loss sample, computed exactly.
+
+    This is the optimal value of the Rockafellar-Uryasev programme: the mean of
+    the worst ``1 - beta`` fraction of the sample, with the observation on the
+    boundary weighted by however much of it falls inside that fraction.
+
+    The tail-risk optimizers report their risk through here rather than reading
+    the solved value of the programme's own auxiliary variables, because those
+    are driven to the risk-minimising point only when the risk measure is the
+    objective. Under ``efficient_risk`` it is a constraint instead, so any
+    feasible value of them is optimal and the solved value describes the bound
+    that was imposed rather than the risk of the portfolio that came back.
